<p>Learn all about the iconique Medi Facials from Dr.B.K.Garg</p>
<p>In the aesthetic industry, when it comes to beauty treatments, a rejuvenating facial has always been the norm. The current trend in facials is moving away from all-purpose facials to problem-solving targeted facials. The latest medi-facial is designed to effectively resurface the skin, reduce fine lines, drives cellular renewal or in short slows the aging process. So ladies, throw out your regular anti-aging products; it’s time to achieve the ultimate ‘youthful glow’ with this revolutionary technique.<br></p>
<p> Medi-facial is a specific skin-pampering technique that combines medicine and aesthetics to provide cosmetic treatments in a spa ambiance. These facials are designed to give consumers instant results for targeted skin concerns, like dark spots, pigmentation and fine lines. Key benefits to look out for? Wrinkle-free, smooth and youthful glowing skin.<br></p>
 <p>Speaking about trending oxygen facial, celebrity makeup artist Gina Brooke says, “Madonna indulges in this lavish beauty treatment before every concert. She always travels with her $14,200 Intraceuticals oxygen machine and also has one in each of her six homes.” When the Madonna Oxylight Facial skincare line first launched in 2017, it instantly grabbed attention in the beauty industry.  Who doesn’t want to know the secret behind flawless skin of 61 years old pop singer?<br></p>
 <p>Indian actress Isha Koppikar says “I have heard of oxygen facials. It is the new beauty mantra in the West and I would love to try it as I’ve heard it can renew skin cells and also fight bacteria that causes acne.”<br></p>
 <p>Medical facials, also known as photo facials incorporate mild peeling agents, advanced types of equipment and specific techniques like microdermabrasion, peels, Photorejuvenation (IPL), LED therapy, microcurrents and a combination of these. They are done under the guidance of a dermatologist. Unlike other beauty facials, they are not based on chemical bleaching principle, rather they induce targeted blend of hyaluronic acid, botanical extracts, antioxidants, peptides and/or vitamins.<br></p>
 <p>Some of the very popular medi-facials are Oxygen facial, Hydro-facial and AHA facial. These facials improve the tone, texture, and collagen production in the skin, thus slowing down the aging process. Its phenomenal anti-aging effect is a reason why celebrities like Madonna are using it to get that perfect red carpet look.<br></p>
 <p>Oxygen facial is popular amongst celebrities like Miranda Kerr, Victoria Beckham, Justin Timberlake, Katy Perry, Wand Madonna. The idea behind this treatment is to stimulate cells to help initiate the production of healthy cells and lift the facial muscles. “Oxygen skin treatment leaves my skin radiant and glowing,” says Victoria's Secret model, Miranda Kerr.<br></p>
 <p>"I use it obviously for facial firming and contouring," Madonna says. "I use it to penetrate the product into my skin. I use it for muscle soreness. I use it for lymphatic drainage. I use it to help reduce cellulite when my muscles are sore”.  Since its Madonna approved, we can only assume it does exactly what it says.<br> 
</p>
<h2>How are Medi Facials different from Normal Everyday Facials?</h2>
<p>There are varieties of beauty facials available at a spa that typically provides a good massage and instant effect but doesn’t penetrate skin deep. While these facials work on the superficial layers, medical facial incorporates advanced devices like mesoporation and ultrasonics to help them penetrate deeper layers giving promising long-lasting results. The goal of general beauty facials is based on relaxation, and while medical facials are more tailored towards true facial rejuvenation. In vampire facial, platelet-rich plasma is injected into the skin for stimulating cellular growth. Is there any other normal facial that can provide such effects?<br></p>
 <p>The main difference between other normal facials and medical facials is that the medical facials are target facials and can be customized to accommodate your skin needs. It could be rectifying aging, dehydrated, sun-damaged, or acne-prone skin. Considering all levels of the skin, various medical techniques can be blended to achieve maximum results.<br></p>
<p>These facial are also proved to be effective when combined with other non-invasive treatments such as injectable dermal fillers or laser resurfacing. Other beauty facials combined with medical-grade ingredients or devices will not only improve the look of your skin but also the long-term health of it too. If you are looking for the best way to improve a skin condition or want to mitigate the signs of aging, then the medical facial is substantially more effective.<br></p>
 <p>As these treatments employ medical-grade tools, they should be performed by a physician or a licensed aesthetician who practices under the supervision of a physician. You must look for licensed skin care professionals with extensive knowledge for safe, effective results.<br>
</p>
